== Attacks and abilities ==
{{For|strategies for defeating Seeker soldiers|Aggressive creature strategies#Seeker soldier}}

=== Ram ===
Brings one claw forward, followed by the other, before slamming forward with their head (100 [[Damage types#Blunt|Blunt]], Tier 4 100 [[Damage types#Chop|Chop]] and 100 Tier 4 [[Damage types#Pickaxe|Pickaxe]] damage). This has an 8-second cooldown and can be used with 4 meters of a player. It hits in a 4-meter 45-degree horizontal arc.

=== Bite ===
Leans back before sweeping downward to clamp the player with their pincers (100 [[Damage types#Pierce|Slash]] damage). This creates a 4-meter 45-degree horizontal arc and can be used every 8 seconds when within 4 meters of a player.

=== Ground slam ===
Brings one arm up and slams it down, followed by the same motion with the other arm (120 [[Damage types#Blunt|Blunt]], Tier 4 100 [[Damage types#Chop|Chop]] and 100 Tier 4 [[Damage types#Pickaxe|Pickaxe]] damage for each hit). This hits in a 4-meter radius circle around each claw and can be used every 12 seconds when within 5 meters of a player.

== Notes ==
Seeker Soldiers are capable of breaking various resources that would otherwise require a [[Black Metal]] tool for the player to break, including black marble deposits, Yggdrasil shoots, and [[Ancient Sword]] and [[Ancient Armor]]. Both their tackle and slam attacks have this property, but not their bite attack. This means that it is theoretically possible for the player to obtain large quantities of both [[Black Marble]] and [[Yggdrasil Wood]] without Black Metal, and it is possible to get much larger quantities of [[Scrap Iron]] outside [[Sunken Crypts]] than with other methods.

This ability to smash rocks should be remembered when fighting Seeker Soldiers. If a player is sniping them from the top of a rock, the Seeker Soldier will often simply demolish the rock.

